.TH MYGREP 3 "2026-09-25" "libmyutils 1.0" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines containing a pattern
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB#include "myfilefunctions.h"\fP
.sp
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR mygrep ()
function reads the file stream pointed to by
.I fp
line by line and collects every line containing the substring
.IR search_str .
On success,
.I *matches
is set to point to a heap-allocated array of heap-allocated strings,
one per matching line. The caller is responsible for freeing each
string in the array and then the array itself.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines found (which may be 0). Returns
\-1 if
.IR fp ,
.IR search_str ,
or
.I matches
is NULL, or if memory allocation fails.
